diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..5d5f8dc 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,6 +2,14 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+## Receiving events
+
+An active webhook receives a POST for each subscribed event on its board. For a generic receiver, the JSON body includes the event’s `id`, `action`, `created_at`, `board`, `creator`, and `eventable` (card or comment). Recognized Slack and Campfire incoming webhook URLs receive a chat message instead. The destination must resolve to a public IP address; redirects are not followed.
+
+Verify `X-Webhook-Signature` against the hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the **raw request body**, using the webhook’s signing secret. `X-Webhook-Timestamp` is the event creation time in UTC, and `Idempotency-Key` is the unique delivery ID.
+
+Fizzy creates one delivery per webhook and event. Once a worker claims it, Fizzy does not retry the POST, even on a timeout: the receiver might have processed it without returning a response. A 2xx response counts as success. Ten or more consecutive failures spanning at least one hour deactivate the webhook; a success or reactivation clears the streak. Delivery history is pruned after one week.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
